A summary of monthly budget figures is shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont, align=left, inner sep=4pt}]
\fill[gray!25] (0,0) rectangle (8,-1);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (8,-4);
\draw (5.2,0) -- (5.2,-4);
\foreach \y in {-1,-2,-3} {\draw (0,\y) -- (8,\y);}
\node[text width=4.8cm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont\bfseries] at (2.6,-0.5) {Monthly Budget Item};
\node[text width=2.4cm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont\bfseries] at (6.6,-0.5) {Amount ($\$$)};
\node[text width=4.8cm] at (2.6,-1.5) {Net Income};
\node[text width=2.4cm] at (6.6,-1.5) {$\$4200$};
\node[text width=4.8cm] at (2.6,-2.5) {Fixed Expenses};
\node[text width=2.4cm] at (6.6,-2.5) {$\$2500$};
\node[text width=4.8cm] at (2.6,-3.5) {Discretionary Expenses};
\node[text width=2.4cm] at (6.6,-3.5) {$\$1150$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the total **annual** budget surplus?
